 atlanta:{label:'ATLANTA MAGAZINE',title:'Atlanta 500.',eyebrow:'RECOGNITION · ATLANTA LEADERSHIP',body:`<p class="living-lead">Part of Atlanta magazine’s community of influential leaders.</p><p>The publication’s business directory describes the Village’s support for entrepreneurs, community crowdfunding, and the Worker’s Equity Fund’s approach to worker ownership.</p><a class="living-link" href="https://www.atlantamagazine.com/news-culture-articles/2026-atlanta-500-business/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the Atlanta 500 profile ↗</a>`},
 morehouse:{label:'MOREHOUSE COLLEGE',title:'Where the path opened.',eyebrow:'EDUCATION · ATLANTA, GEORGIA',body:`<p class="living-lead">Morehouse College. Business administration. A commitment to building something that matters.</p><p>At Morehouse, a curiosity about money became a study of accounting and the systems behind capital. Those years opened doors to experiences at the Federal Reserve, Google, and Goldman Sachs—and to the beginnings of Village Micro Fund.</p><p>The framed Morehouse piece represents education and the foundation of the journey.</p><a class="living-link" href="https://www.atlantamagazine.com/news-culture-articles/2024-atlanta-500-business/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the profile and education background ↗</a>`},
